                <pb facs="0846" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/27a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-28T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 28,
                                1918, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>571. For Finnish Legation: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Presented credentials today to Secretary Lansing who, expressing personal views, said America
                            recognizes that Finland has set up a <hi rendition="#italic">de
                                facto</hi> government. He also assured us of America’s sympathy for
                            Finland’s aspiration for independence. President unable to receive us
                            pending internal disturbances in Finland. Secretary Lansing advised us to wait until
                            authority of Finnish government firmly established whereupon audience
                            with President would probably follow and recognition discussed. Please
                            transmit above to Finnish government. Reuter, Ignatius.</p></quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
